<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Bussa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New Bussa is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> State, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, built in the 1960s to house the people of old Bussa and nearby villages displaced by the reservoir of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kainji-dam">Kainji Dam</a>. It is the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borgu">Borgu</a> and the main town of the Kainji Lake area, with its national park and freshwater fisheries research.</p></div>
